          "data": {
            "text/markdown": "<span class=\"markdown prose dark:prose-invert contents\"><h2 id=\"challenge-2-binary-search\">Challenge 2: Binary search</h2>\n<span class=\"paragraph\">If the records are <strong>sorted by <code>Field_ID</code></strong>, we can do much better. Jump to the middle record. Is the target ID higher or lower? Discard half the list. Repeat. This is a <strong>binary search</strong>: <code>O(log n)</code> \u2014 at one million records, it takes roughly 20 comparisons instead of one million.</span>\n<span class=\"paragraph\">The cost: the data must be sorted first.</span>\n<h3 id=\"task\">Task</h3>\n<span class=\"paragraph\">Complete <code>binary_search_yield(sorted_field_list, target_id)</code>. Assume the input is already sorted by <code>Field_ID</code> in ascending order. Return the <code>Annual_yield</code> of the matching record, or <code>None</code> if not found.</span>\n<blockquote>\n<span class=\"paragraph\">\u26a0\ufe0f Do not change the function name <code>binary_search_yield</code>.</span>\n</blockquote>\n<h3 id=\"expected-outputs\">Expected outputs</h3>\n<span class=\"paragraph\"><strong>Input 1:</strong>\n<div class=\"language-python codehilite\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"n\">sorted_sample</span> <span class=\"o\">=</span> <span class=\"nb\">sorted</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"n\">maji_ndogo_sample</span><span class=\"p\">,</span> <span class=\"n\">key</span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"k\">lambda</span> <span class=\"n\">f</span><span class=\"p\">:</span> <span class=\"n\">f</span><span class=\"p\">[</span><span class=\"s1\">&#39;Field_ID&#39;</span><span class=\"p\">])</span>\n<span class=\"n\">binary_search_yield</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"n\">sorted_sample</span><span class=\"p\">,</span> <span class=\"mi\">30629</span><span class=\"p\">)</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<code>1.0699</code></span>\n<span class=\"paragraph\"><strong>Input 2:</strong>\n<div class=\"language-python codehilite\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"n\">sorted_sample</span> <span class=\"o\">=</span> <span class=\"nb\">sorted</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"n\">maji_ndogo_sample</span><span class=\"p\">,</span> <span class=\"n\">key</span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"k\">lambda</span> <span class=\"n\">f</span><span class=\"p\">:</span> <span class=\"n\">f</span><span class=\"p\">[</span><span class=\"s1\">&#39;Field_ID&#39;</span><span class=\"p\">])</span>\n<span class=\"nb\">print</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"n\">binary_search_yield</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"n\">sorted_sample</span><span class=\"p\">,</span> <span class=\"mi\">11111</span><span class=\"p\">))</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<code>None</code></span></span>"
          }
