            "text/markdown": "<span class=\"markdown prose dark:prose-invert contents\"><h2 id=\"challenge-5-lambda-and-map-projecting-harvests\">Challenge 5: Lambda and map \u2014 projecting harvests</h2>\n<span class=\"paragraph\">If <code>filter()</code> decides which items to <em>keep</em>, <code>map()</code> transforms <em>every</em> item. The Ministry of Agriculture wants a quick harvest projection for each field: <code>Plot_size</code> \u00d7 <code>Standard_yield</code>, rounded to 2 decimal places.</span>\n<h3 id=\"task\">Task</h3>\n<span class=\"paragraph\">Complete <code>project_harvests(field_list)</code>. Use <code>map()</code> and a <code>lambda</code> to compute each field's projected yield (<code>Plot_size * Standard_yield</code>, rounded to 2 decimals). Return the result as a list.</span>\n<blockquote>\n<span class=\"paragraph\">\u26a0\ufe0f Do not change the function name <code>project_harvests</code>.</span>\n</blockquote>\n<h3 id=\"expected-outputs\">Expected outputs</h3>\n<span class=\"paragraph\"><strong>Input 1:</strong> <code>project_harvests(maji_ndogo_sample)</code> \u2192 <code>[0.75, 1.07, 2.21, 1.28, 0.83]</code></span>\n<span class=\"paragraph\"><strong>Input 2:</strong> <code>project_harvests(maji_ndogo_sample[2:4])</code> \u2192 <code>[2.21, 1.28]</code></span></span>"
